{
  "version": 1,
  "_schema": "despia-style-overrides-v1",
  "_note": [
    "THE STYLE-OVERRIDE PLANE. A component's ATTRIBUTES are its data contract; its OVERRIDES",
    "are its style contract - the typed knobs a consumer may turn on ONE INSTANCE without",
    "forking the component or reaching global CSS. A component declares them in its head",
    "(<override as=\"radius\" type=\"length\" default=\"12\"/>), a consumer sets them on the",
    "usage tag (override:radius=\"6\", override:radius=\"{{ expr }}\"), and the component's own",
    "markup spends them wherever it chooses (radius=\"{{ dsx.override.radius }}\"), at any",
    "depth. Nothing auto-applies: declaring an override does nothing until the component's",
    "markup reads it, which is what keeps the contract enumerable and the pixels owned by the",
    "component author.",
    "",
    "Three pure laws live here, and every renderer implements all three identically:",
    "",
    "  split   - which usage-site attributes ARE overrides. `override:<name>` where <name> is",
    "            an identifier (dsx.override.<name> must be a legal member read). The matched",
    "            key leaves the props plane entirely. `on:` handlers are never overrides, a",
    "            bare `override:` or a non-identifier tail is NOT an override (it stays an",
    "            ordinary - and lint-flagged - attribute), and the platform-suffix fold runs",
    "            FIRST, so override:radius:ios reaches the split as override:radius on iOS and",
    "            not at all elsewhere. Names on the `reserved` list below can therefore never",
    "            be override names: the fold consumes them as platform tags.",
    "",
    "  resolve - what a declared override is WORTH given a raw consumer value. Fail-open,",
    "            never throwing: unset, empty and invalid all fall back to the declaration's",
    "            default, itself coerced by the same rule; a default that fails its own type",
    "            resolves null. Types are the style catalog's control vocabulary plus `css`:",
    "            number (strict full-string numeric, clamped to min/max), length (numeric ->",
    "            number + clamp, else a unit/keyword/functional string), color (#RGB/#RGBA/",
    "            #RRGGBB/#AARRGGBB hex, rgb()/rgba()/hsl()/hsla(), or a bare token name),",
    "            enum (exactly one of options), multiEnum (whitespace-separated members of",
    "            options, normalized to single spaces), boolean ('true'/'false' or a real",
    "            boolean), gradient/ratio/text (scalar string without ';', '{', '}'), css (a",
    "            raw declaration list, verbatim after outer trim). Unknown declared types",
    "            resolve as text - lint owns rejecting the declaration.",
    "",
    "  read    - what dsx.override.<name> RETURNS inside the instance. Resolution chain:",
    "            the instance item scope's __overrides dict (the tag door), then the",
    "            store's dsx.override var (the mount/update door), then the declaration",
    "            default. Every read passes through resolve, so a live write of garbage",
    "            degrades to the default instead of poisoning the pixels. An UNDECLARED name",
    "            reads null (contract-first; lint errors at the usage site). The whole-plane",
    "            read `dsx.override` returns the declared contract resolved - never raw,",
    "            never undeclared keys.",
    "",
    "Runners - three implementations, all three execute this file:",
    "  TS     - OpenSource/Web/packages/kernel/test/style-overrides-conformance.test.ts (per-PR)",
    "  Kotlin - :core StyleOverridesConformanceTest (per-PR, gradle, SDK-free)",
    "  Swift  - StyleOverridesConformance (per-PR via swift_conformance_run_test.rb on the",
    "           linux lane, and RecordMain.swift on the record lane)"
  ],
  "identifier": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$",
  "reserved": [
    "ios",
    "android",
    "web",
    "watch",
    "wear",
    "macos",
    "windows",
    "linux",
    "native",
    "desktop"
  ],
  "split": [
    {
      "name": "a plain attribute stays a prop",
      "attrs": {
        "label": "Hello"
      },
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {},
        "props": {
          "label": "Hello"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "override:<name> leaves the props plane",
      "attrs": {
        "label": "Hello",
        "override:radius": "6"
      },
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {
          "radius": "6"
        },
        "props": {
          "label": "Hello"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "several overrides split independently",
      "attrs": {
        "override:radius": "6",
        "override:tint": "accent",
        "title": "x"
      },
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {
          "radius": "6",
          "tint": "accent"
        },
        "props": {
          "title": "x"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "an on: handler is never an override",
      "attrs": {
        "on:tap": "dsx.event('tap')",
        "override:radius": "6"
      },
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {
          "radius": "6"
        },
        "props": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a bound override value rides through untouched",
      "attrs": {
        "override:radius": "{{ dsx.variable.r }}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {
          "radius": "{{ dsx.variable.r }}"
        },
        "props": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "bare override: with no name is not an override",
      "attrs": {
        "override:": "6"
      },
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {},
        "props": {
          "override:": "6"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a non-identifier tail is not an override",
      "attrs": {
        "override:a.b": "6",
        "override:a:b": "7",
        "override:9lives": "8"
      },
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {},
        "props": {
          "override:a.b": "6",
          "override:a:b": "7",
          "override:9lives": "8"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "underscore-led identifiers are legal override names",
      "attrs": {
        "override:_edge": "1"
      },
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {
          "_edge": "1"
        },
        "props": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "the word override alone is an ordinary attribute",
      "attrs": {
        "override": "yes"
      },
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {},
        "props": {
          "override": "yes"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "empty attrs split to empty planes",
      "attrs": {},
      "expect": {
        "overrides": {},
        "props": {}
      }
    }
  ],
  "resolve": [
    {
      "name": "text: value passes through",
      "decl": {
        "type": "text"
      },
      "raw": "hello",
      "expect": "hello"
    },
    {
      "name": "text: unset falls to default",
      "decl": {
        "type": "text",
        "default": "hi"
      },
      "expect": "hi"
    },
    {
      "name": "text: empty string falls to default",
      "decl": {
        "type": "text",
        "default": "hi"
      },
      "raw": "",
      "expect": "hi"
    },
    {
      "name": "text: whitespace-only raw is empty and falls to default",
      "decl": {
        "type": "text",
        "default": "hi"
      },
      "raw": "   ",
      "expect": "hi"
    },
    {
      "name": "text: unset with no default is null",
      "decl": {
        "type": "text"
      },
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "text: a number coerces to its string",
      "decl": {
        "type": "text"
      },
      "raw": 5,
      "expect": "5"
    },
    {
      "name": "text: outer whitespace trims",
      "decl": {
        "type": "text"
      },
      "raw": "  pad  ",
      "expect": "pad"
    },
    {
      "name": "missing type reads as text",
      "decl": {},
      "raw": "free",
      "expect": "free"
    },
    {
      "name": "unknown type reads as text (lint owns the declaration)",
      "decl": {
        "type": "mystery"
      },
      "raw": "v",
      "expect": "v"
    },
    {
      "name": "number: numeric string coerces to a number",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number"
      },
      "raw": "6",
      "expect": 6
    },
    {
      "name": "number: a real number passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number"
      },
      "raw": 6.5,
      "expect": 6.5
    },
    {
      "name": "number: decimals parse",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number"
      },
      "raw": "12.5",
      "expect": 12.5
    },
    {
      "name": "number: negatives parse",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number"
      },
      "raw": "-4",
      "expect": -4
    },
    {
      "name": "number: a leading dot parses",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number"
      },
      "raw": ".5",
      "expect": 0.5
    },
    {
      "name": "number: a unit suffix is NOT a number",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "default": "3"
      },
      "raw": "6px",
      "expect": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "number: garbage falls to default",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "default": "3"
      },
      "raw": "abc",
      "expect": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "number: a boolean is not a number",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "default": "3"
      },
      "raw": true,
      "expect": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "number: min clamps",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "min": 0
      },
      "raw": "-2",
      "expect": 0
    },
    {
      "name": "number: max clamps",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "max": 48
      },
      "raw": "96",
      "expect": 48
    },
    {
      "name": "number: in-range value is untouched",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "min": 0,
        "max": 48
      },
      "raw": "12",
      "expect": 12
    },
    {
      "name": "number: the default itself coerces",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "default": "12"
      },
      "expect": 12
    },
    {
      "name": "number: an invalid default resolves null",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "default": "abc"
      },
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "number: the default clamps too",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "default": "96",
        "max": 48
      },
      "expect": 48
    },
    {
      "name": "number: zero survives as zero, not as unset",
      "decl": {
        "type": "number",
        "default": "3"
      },
      "raw": "0",
      "expect": 0
    },
    {
      "name": "length: numeric coerces to a number",
      "decl": {
        "type": "length"
      },
      "raw": "6",
      "expect": 6
    },
    {
      "name": "length: numeric clamps to min/max",
      "decl": {
        "type": "length",
        "min": 4,
        "max": 20
      },
      "raw": "48",
      "expect": 20
    },
    {
      "name": "length: a unit string passes through",
      "decl": {
        "type": "length"
      },
      "raw": "12px",
      "expect": "12px"
    },
    {
      "name": "length: a keyword passes through",
      "decl": {
        "type": "length"
      },
      "raw": "fit",
      "expect": "fit"
    },
    {
      "name": "length: a functional value passes through",
      "decl": {
        "type": "length"
      },
      "raw": "calc(100% - 8px)",
      "expect": "calc(100% - 8px)"
    },
    {
      "name": "length: a declaration list is not a length",
      "decl": {
        "type": "length",
        "default": "8"
      },
      "raw": "radius: 6; padding: 2",
      "expect": 8
    },
    {
      "name": "length: empty falls to default and the default coerces",
      "decl": {
        "type": "length",
        "default": "12"
      },
      "raw": "",
      "expect": 12
    },
    {
      "name": "color: six-digit hex passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color"
      },
      "raw": "#6C5CE7",
      "expect": "#6C5CE7"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: three-digit hex passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color"
      },
      "raw": "#FFF",
      "expect": "#FFF"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: eight-digit hex passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color"
      },
      "raw": "#806C5CE7",
      "expect": "#806C5CE7"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: four-digit hex passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color"
      },
      "raw": "#8FFF",
      "expect": "#8FFF"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: five-digit hex is invalid",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color",
        "default": "accent"
      },
      "raw": "#12345",
      "expect": "accent"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: non-hex garbage after # is invalid",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color",
        "default": "accent"
      },
      "raw": "#GGHHII",
      "expect": "accent"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: rgb() passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color"
      },
      "raw": "rgb(10, 20, 30)",
      "expect": "rgb(10, 20, 30)"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: functional value spanning a newline passes (prefix semantics, all three runners)",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color"
      },
      "raw": "rgb(10,\n 20, 30)",
      "expect": "rgb(10,\n 20, 30)"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: rgba() passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color"
      },
      "raw": "rgba(0,0,0,0.4)",
      "expect": "rgba(0,0,0,0.4)"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: hsl() passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color"
      },
      "raw": "hsl(200, 50%, 40%)",
      "expect": "hsl(200, 50%, 40%)"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: a bare token name passes (the semantic vocabulary)",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color"
      },
      "raw": "secondaryGroupedBackground",
      "expect": "secondaryGroupedBackground"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: a token name may not carry digits or spaces",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color",
        "default": "accent"
      },
      "raw": "12px",
      "expect": "accent"
    },
    {
      "name": "color: an unbalanced functional form is invalid",
      "decl": {
        "type": "color",
        "default": "accent"
      },
      "raw": "rgb(1, 2",
      "expect": "accent"
    },
    {
      "name": "enum: a member passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "enum",
        "options": "raised cut flat"
      },
      "raw": "cut",
      "expect": "cut"
    },
    {
      "name": "enum: a non-member falls to default",
      "decl": {
        "type": "enum",
        "options": "raised cut flat",
        "default": "raised"
      },
      "raw": "fancy",
      "expect": "raised"
    },
    {
      "name": "enum: matching is case-sensitive",
      "decl": {
        "type": "enum",
        "options": "raised cut",
        "default": "raised"
      },
      "raw": "CUT",
      "expect": "raised"
    },
    {
      "name": "enum: unset falls to default",
      "decl": {
        "type": "enum",
        "options": "raised cut",
        "default": "cut"
      },
      "expect": "cut"
    },
    {
      "name": "enum: no options means nothing matches",
      "decl": {
        "type": "enum",
        "default": "x"
      },
      "raw": "x",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "multiEnum: members normalize to single spaces",
      "decl": {
        "type": "multiEnum",
        "options": "bold italic underline"
      },
      "raw": "bold   underline",
      "expect": "bold underline"
    },
    {
      "name": "multiEnum: one bad token rejects the whole value",
      "decl": {
        "type": "multiEnum",
        "options": "bold italic",
        "default": "bold"
      },
      "raw": "bold shiny",
      "expect": "bold"
    },
    {
      "name": "multiEnum: a single member passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "multiEnum",
        "options": "bold italic"
      },
      "raw": "italic",
      "expect": "italic"
    },
    {
      "name": "boolean: the string true is true",
      "decl": {
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "raw": "true",
      "expect": true
    },
    {
      "name": "boolean: the string false is false",
      "decl": {
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "raw": "false",
      "expect": false
    },
    {
      "name": "boolean: a real boolean passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "raw": true,
      "expect": true
    },
    {
      "name": "boolean: case matters - TRUE is invalid",
      "decl": {
        "type": "boolean",
        "default": "false"
      },
      "raw": "TRUE",
      "expect": false
    },
    {
      "name": "boolean: a number is not a boolean",
      "decl": {
        "type": "boolean",
        "default": "true"
      },
      "raw": 1,
      "expect": true
    },
    {
      "name": "boolean: unset falls to the coerced default",
      "decl": {
        "type": "boolean",
        "default": "true"
      },
      "expect": true
    },
    {
      "name": "ratio: a ratio string passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "ratio"
      },
      "raw": "16:9",
      "expect": "16:9"
    },
    {
      "name": "gradient: a gradient string passes",
      "decl": {
        "type": "gradient"
      },
      "raw": "linear-gradient(180deg, #000, #fff)",
      "expect": "linear-gradient(180deg, #000, #fff)"
    },
    {
      "name": "css: a declaration list passes verbatim after outer trim",
      "decl": {
        "type": "css"
      },
      "raw": " border-radius: 6px; background: red ",
      "expect": "border-radius: 6px; background: red"
    },
    {
      "name": "css: braces are refused (a declaration list, never a rule)",
      "decl": {
        "type": "css",
        "default": "opacity: 1"
      },
      "raw": ".x { color: red }",
      "expect": "opacity: 1"
    },
    {
      "name": "css: empty falls to default",
      "decl": {
        "type": "css",
        "default": "opacity: 1"
      },
      "raw": "",
      "expect": "opacity: 1"
    },
    {
      "name": "css: unset with no default is null",
      "decl": {
        "type": "css"
      },
      "expect": null
    }
  ],
  "read": [
    {
      "name": "an unset override reads its coerced default",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "radius",
          "type": "length",
          "default": "12"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {},
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.radius",
          "value": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a consumer value beats the default and is coerced",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "radius",
          "type": "length",
          "default": "12"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "radius": "6"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.radius",
          "value": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an invalid consumer value degrades to the default",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "radius",
          "type": "number",
          "default": "12",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 48
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "radius": "huge"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.radius",
          "value": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an out-of-range consumer value clamps",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "radius",
          "type": "number",
          "default": "12",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 48
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "radius": "96"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.radius",
          "value": 48
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an undeclared name reads null",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "radius",
          "type": "length",
          "default": "12"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "ghost": "6"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.ghost",
          "value": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "overrides and attributes are separate planes",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "tint",
          "type": "color",
          "default": "accent"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "tint": "#FF0000"
      },
      "attributes": {
        "tint": "data-plane"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.tint",
          "value": "#FF0000"
        },
        {
          "expr": "dsx.attribute.tint",
          "value": "data-plane"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "the whole-plane read returns the resolved declared contract",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "radius",
          "type": "length",
          "default": "12"
        },
        {
          "as": "tint",
          "type": "color",
          "default": "accent"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "radius": "6",
        "ghost": "x"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.radius",
          "value": 6
        },
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.tint",
          "value": "accent"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a boolean override is a real boolean in expressions",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "glass",
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": "true"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "glass": "false"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.glass",
          "value": false
        },
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.glass ? 'on' : 'off'",
          "value": "off"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a number override does arithmetic",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "pad",
          "type": "number",
          "default": "8"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "pad": "10"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.pad + 2",
          "value": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an enum override honors its options",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "surface",
          "type": "enum",
          "options": "raised cut flat",
          "default": "raised"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "surface": "velvet"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.surface",
          "value": "raised"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a css override arrives verbatim",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "extra",
          "type": "css"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "extra": "border-radius: 6px; opacity: 0.9"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.extra",
          "value": "border-radius: 6px; opacity: 0.9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an empty consumer value means unset, so the default answers",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "tint",
          "type": "color",
          "default": "accent"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "tint": ""
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.tint",
          "value": "accent"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "the store var door answers when the item scope has no dict",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "radius",
          "type": "length",
          "default": "12"
        }
      ],
      "storeOverrides": {
        "radius": "20"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.radius",
          "value": 20
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "the item scope beats the store var (the tag door wins)",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "as": "radius",
          "type": "length",
          "default": "12"
        }
      ],
      "overrides": {
        "radius": "6"
      },
      "storeOverrides": {
        "radius": "20"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.radius",
          "value": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "no declarations means every read is null",
      "declarations": [],
      "overrides": {
        "radius": "6"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "expr": "dsx.override.radius",
          "value": null
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
